whether you're a vegetarian vegan or  just looking to add more vegetables into  your diet you've got to try this healthy  veggie burger recipes you get to satisfy  your craving for a burger but without  the saturated fats so these burgers are  high in protein and fiber but low in fat  and hey they can be gluten-free as well  and the best part about these burgers is  that they're extremely versatile and  easy to make so I'm going to show you  three variations of my favorite veggie  burgers so let's start with the curried  chickpea burger this burger is packed  with spices such as Kayne cumin and also  Korean and you get the nutty taste of  chickpeas as well so what have used our  one can of chickpeas wash and drained  two garlic cloves minced 2 tablespoons  of olive oil 1/2 a teaspoon of cumin 1/2  a teaspoon of curry powder and half a  teaspoon of cayenne pepper add the  chickpeas into a food processor or  blender along with the garlic all the  spices and 1 tablespoon of oil blend  until you get a thick mixture using your  hands form the mixture into four burger  patties each patty has about 112  calories the next recipe has to be my  favorite because it combines both  mushrooms and also black beans  the thing is mushrooms are surprisingly  similar to the texture of meat when  cooked so eating this mushroom black  bean burger will not make you miss the  taste of a regular meat burger what I've  used are 3/4 cup of fresh mushrooms  finely diced 3 quat a can of black beans  rinsed and drained 2 tablespoons of  olive oil 1/2 a cup of onion diced 1  garlic clove minced 1 tbsp of green  onions roughly chopped half a teaspoon  of cumin salt and pepper to taste  so the key step here is to saute the  mushrooms and onions before mixing it  together with the beans which will  infuse much more flavor to the patties  so the first step here is to saute the  garlic  and onion for three to five minutes  until they are soft and fragrant then  add in the chopped mushrooms green  onions and cumin continue to saute for  another five minutes or until the  mushrooms are cooked through then remove  from heat and allow the mixture to cool  down in a bowl roughly mash the black  beans I like to keep them chunky then  combine the mashed black beans with the  onion and mushroom mixture and flavor it  with salt and pepper mix until all the  ingredients are well combined again  using your hands shape the mixture into  four equal patties about 3/4 to 1 inch  thick mushrooms pack plenty of flavors  and texture and the black beans makes  this burger much high in fiber and also  protein which will keep you fuller for  much longer  each patty has about 112 calories and my  final recipe is the tofu burger tofu is  a staple ingredient in most vegan or  vegetarian diets it's extremely  versatile and it takes on the flavor of  whatever ingredients you combine it with  this tofu burger packs on the flavors  from the garlic and onions plus it has  the additional neutron boost from char  seeds  what abuse are one block of extra firm  tofu half a cup of onion diced 1 tbsp of  green onions roughly chopped and 1 part  of cha mixture which is a combination of  1 tablespoon of chia seeds with 3  tablespoons of water 2 tablespoons of  soy sauce 1 tablespoon of oil 1 garlic  clove minced and salt and pepper to  taste  blend the tofu along with the rest of  the ingredients onions green onions  garlic salt and pepper charm mixture and  soya sauce blend until you form a tofu  paste next gently form the tofu mixture  into patties pressing everything  together to form round patties about 3/4  to 1 inch thick this should make you  about 4 patties  this tofu burger it's very light fluffy  and easy to be eaten each Patsy has  about 104 calories on a nonstick pan  heat 1 tablespoon of oil under  medium-high heat then cook the patties  on both sides until they are slightly  Brown and crunchy  just for about 5 minutes remove from  heat and set aside now let's put these  burgers together you can even use  English muffins or mini burger buns so  I've topped my burgers with baby spinach  and sliced tomatoes choose any  vegetables of your choice  just look at them they are healthy  delicious and even perfect to be served  at a party snack trust me you will not  leave missing your regular meat burgers  after trying one of these they are moist  tender and packed with flavor you got to  try them make them snap and share your  pictures with me  tag me as a journalist or official and  hashtag it chase your recipes let me  know which is your favorite in the  comments below ok  be sure to snap because I want to see  all your veggie burger creations don't  forget to like this video share this  video and hit the subscribe button if  you haven't yet done it turn on your  notification button so that you would  get notified every time I upload a new  healthy and delicious recipe all the  best
 

